{"name":"Traffic Light Green","hex":"#8c9900","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"traffic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Moving pedestrians or vehicles, or the flux or passage thereof.","The commercial transportation or exchange of goods, or the movement of passengers or people."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pass goods and commodities from one person to another for an equivalent in goods or money; to buy or sell goods.","To trade meanly or mercenarily; to bargain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traffic"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"X11 color names","blocks":[{"text":"In computing, on the X Window System, X11 color names are represented in a simple text file, which maps certain strings to RGB color values. It was traditionally shipped with every X11 installation, hence the name, and is usually located in <X11root>/lib/X11/rgb.txt. The web colors list is descended from it but differs for certain color names."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X11_color_names","wikidata":"Q376249"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green","wikidata":"Q19847180"},{"title":"Traffic light","blocks":[{"text":"Traffic lights, traffic signals, or stoplights – also known as robots in South Africa, Zambia, and Namibia – are signalling devices positioned at road intersections, pedestrian crossings, and other locations to control the flow of traffic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Modern_British_LED_Traffic_Light.jpg/330px-Modern_British_LED_Traffic_Light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light","wikidata":"Q8004"},{"title":"Traffic","blocks":[{"text":"Traffic is the movement of vehicles and pedestrians along land routes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Crossing_the_Hudson_River_on_the_George_Washington_Bridge_from_Fort_Lee%2C_New_Jersey_to_Manhattan%2C_New_York_%287237796950%29.jpg/330px-Crossing_the_Hudson_River_on_the_George_Washington_Bridge_from_Fort_Lee%2C_New_Jersey_to_Manhattan%2C_New_York_%287237796950%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic","wikidata":"Q4323994"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikiped